# New Environment Variables

When introducing a **new environment variable** (used in code via `process.env`, `ConfigService`, or config modules), update all of the following:

1. **`.env.example`**  
   Add the variable with a placeholder or comment. Document purpose if non-obvious (e.g. comma-separated list, optional).

2. **`helm/values.yaml`**  
   Add the variable under `secrets.secrets[].data` (app-secret) with an appropriate value or placeholder (e.g. `'changeme'`, empty string, or env-specific value).

3. **`helm/values-staging.yaml`**  
   Add the same variable under `secrets.secrets[].data` with a staging-appropriate value or placeholder.

Keep variable names and ordering consistent across these files. Use SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE for env keys (see camelcase rule exception).
